{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And you shall appoint.</b> From the root פקיד." "<b>Oil of the lamp.</b> Some say that he would carry the oil of the lamp for one night, and likewise the regular meal-offering. But the correct view in my eyes is that he is appointed over it, to provide the oil of the lamp; and the meaning of כלי (vessel) is likewise כלי שמן המשחה (vessel of anointing oil) and כלי הקטורת (vessel of incense) — for the Kohathites." "And the meaning of <b>the charge of all the Tabernacle:</b> for he also has charges in the Tabernacle and in all its vessels together with his brother Ithamar. Only by virtue of the greatness of Eleazar's rank, he alone was appointed over the oil, the incense, and the meal-offering."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:16.423669836Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}